+# Sales Forecasting Module — Starter Prompt & Specification
+
+**Date:** 2026-05-24  
+**Module:** `sales_forecasting` (`@open-mercato/sales-forecasting`)  
+**Status:** In progress (MVP implemented)  
+**Depends on:** `sales` (order revenue history), `directory` (tenant/org scope)
+
+## TLDR
+
+Add an optional Open Mercato package that aggregates historical **sales order revenue** into time buckets, runs pluggable forecasting engines (baseline + ARIMA via open-source npm), persists forecast runs for audit, and exposes admin UI + API for revenue planning.
+
+## Overview
+
+Sales and operations teams need forward-looking revenue views without exporting data to spreadsheets or external BI tools. This module sits on top of existing `sales_orders` data, respects multi-tenant organization scoping, and keeps forecasting logic isolated in a dedicated package so core `sales` stays transactional.
+
+## Problem Statement
+
+- Open Mercato has rich sales documents (orders, quotes, invoices) but no first-class **time-series forecasting**.
+- Teams currently rely on external tools (Excel, Python notebooks, Prophet) with manual exports — breaking tenancy, RBAC, and audit trails.
+- Embedding heavy ML in core would bloat the platform; a **separate ejectable module** matches the official-modules pattern.
+
+## Proposed Solution (MVP)
+
+1. **History aggregation** — bucket `SalesOrder.grandTotalGrossAmount` by day/week/month using `COALESCE(placed_at, created_at)`.
+2. **Forecast engines** (registry pattern):
+   - `naive` — repeat last observed value
+   - `moving_average` — windowed mean (default window 3)
+   - `seasonal_naive` — repeat value from one season ago (weekly/monthly)
+   - `arima` — AutoARIMA via [`arima`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/arima) (MIT, WASM, Node + browser)
+3. **Persistence** — `sales_forecast_runs` stores parameters, historical points, forecast points, and diagnostics.
+4. **API** — `POST /api/sales_forecasting/predict` (on-demand), `GET /api/sales_forecasting/runs` (paginated history).
+5. **Admin UI** — `/backend/sales_forecasting` with metric/horizon/engine selectors and results table.
+
+## Open-Source Forecasting Landscape (evaluation)
+
+| Library | Runtime | License | Fit for Open Mercato | Notes |
+|---------|---------|---------|----------------------|-------|
+| [**arima**](https://github.com/zemlyansky/arima) | Node (WASM) | MIT | **MVP choice** | ARIMA/SARIMA/AutoARIMA, no native deps, ~16k weekly npm downloads |
+| [**@sipemu/anofox-forecast**](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sipemu/anofox-forecast) | Node (WASM) | MIT | Phase 2 | 50+ models, AutoEnsemble; newer, smaller ecosystem |
+| [**Prophet**](https://github.com/facebook/prophet) | Python | MIT | Sidecar / worker | Best for strong seasonality + holidays; requires Python service or queue worker |
+| **statsmodels** (ARIMA/ETS) | Python | BSD | Sidecar | Common in Django stacks; not in-process for TS monolith |
+| **simple-statistics** / hand-rolled | Node | Various | Baselines only | Good for naive/MA; insufficient alone for seasonality |
+
+**Recommendation:** Ship **in-process baselines + `arima` AutoARIMA** in MVP. Add optional **Prophet sidecar** (HTTP worker or queue job) in a follow-up spec when holiday calendars and changepoint detection are required.
+
+## Architecture
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+│  @open-mercato/sales-forecasting (package)                  │
+│  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌──────────────────────────────────┐  │
+│  │ aggregateSales  │→ │ forecast engines (registry)      │  │
+│  │ History (sales) │  │ naive | moving_avg | seasonal |  │  │
+│  └────────┬────────┘  │ arima (npm arima)                │  │
+│           │           └──────────────┬───────────────────┘  │
+│           │                          │                      │
+│           ▼                          ▼                      │
+│  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │
+│  │ SalesForecastRun entity + forecastService              │ │
+│  └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
+│           │ API predict / runs  │  Backend UI page         │
+└───────────┴─────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘
+            │ reads SalesOrder (@open-mercato/core)
+            ▼
+```
+
+- **Package:** `packages/sales-forecasting` — mirrors `webhooks` layout.
+- **Registration:** `{ id: 'sales_forecasting', from: '@open-mercato/sales-forecasting' }` in `apps/mercato/src/modules.ts`.
+- **RBAC:** `sales_forecasting.view`, `sales_forecasting.run`, `sales_forecasting.manage`.
+
+## Data Models
+
+### `SalesForecastRun` (`sales_forecast_runs`)
+
+| Field | Type | Description |
+|-------|------|-------------|
+| `id` | uuid | PK |
+| `tenant_id`, `organization_id` | uuid | Scope |
+| `metric` | text | `revenue_gross` (MVP) |
+| `granularity` | text | `day` \| `week` \| `month` |
+| `engine` | text | Engine key |
+| `horizon` | int | Forecast steps |
+| `history_points` | jsonb | `{ periodStart, value }[]` |
+| `forecast_points` | jsonb | `{ periodStart, value, lower?, upper? }[]` |
+| `diagnostics` | jsonb | Engine metadata, point counts, errors |
+| `created_by_user_id` | uuid? | Actor |
+| `created_at`, `updated_at` | timestamptz | Audit |
+
+## API Contracts
+
+### `POST /api/sales_forecasting/predict`
+
+**Auth:** `sales_forecasting.run`
+
+**Body:**
+```json
+{
+  "metric": "revenue_gross",
+  "granularity": "week",
+  "engine": "arima",
+  "horizon": 12,
+  "historyPeriods": 52,
+  "engineOptions": { "auto": true }
+}
+```
+
+**Response:**
+```json
+{
+  "runId": "uuid",
+  "engine": "arima",
+  "history": [{ "periodStart": "2025-06-02", "value": 12000.5 }],
+  "forecast": [{ "periodStart": "2026-05-26", "value": 13500.2 }],
+  "diagnostics": { "historyCount": 52, "minimumPoints": 8 }
+}
+```
+
+### `GET /api/sales_forecasting/runs`
+
+**Auth:** `sales_forecasting.view` — paginated list of persisted runs.
+
+## UI/UX
+
+- **Nav:** Sales group → “Sales forecasting” (`/backend/sales_forecasting`).
+- Controls: granularity, horizon, engine, history depth.
+- Results: historical + forecast tables; future chart widget (dashboard injection) out of MVP scope.
+
+## Risks & Impact Review
+
+| Risk | Severity | Mitigation | Residual |
+|------|----------|------------|----------|
+| Sparse order history → poor forecasts | Medium | Minimum point guard; clear diagnostics | Users must interpret low-data warnings |
+| ARIMA WASM perf on large horizons | Low | Cap horizon (e.g. 52); run async in phase 2 | Large tenants may need queue worker |
+| Currency mixing | Medium | MVP: single-currency org assumption; filter by dominant `currency_code` in phase 2 | Multi-currency orgs see blended series |
+| Deleted/cancelled orders skew history | Medium | Exclude `deleted_at` + optional status filter in phase 2 | MVP includes all non-deleted orders |
+
+## Phase 2 (out of MVP)
+
+- Deal pipeline weighted forecast (`customer_deals` × stage probability)
+- Prophet / anofox sidecar + ensemble picker
+- Dashboard widget + AI assistant tool
+- Scheduled refresh via `scheduler` module
+- Confidence intervals from ARIMA variance
+
+## Agent Starter Prompt
+
+Use this block when implementing or extending the module:
+
+```
+You are adding or extending the Open Mercato `sales_forecasting` module in
+`packages/sales-forecasting/`.
+
+Before coding:
+1. Read `.ai/specs/2026-05-24-sales-forecasting-module-starter-prompt.md`
+2. Read `packages/sales-forecasting/AGENTS.md`
+3. Mirror patterns from `packages/webhooks` (package layout, ACL, setup, API scope helpers)
+4. Read `packages/core/src/modules/sales/data/entities.ts` for SalesOrder fields
+
+Rules:
+- MUST depend on `sales` module data via DI (`SalesOrder`) — no duplicated order tables
+- MUST scope all queries by tenantId + organizationId (see api/helpers.ts)
+- MUST register engines in `lib/engines/registry.ts` — no ad hoc model calls from routes
+- Prefer MIT/Apache OSS engines runnable in Node; document Python sidecars in spec only
+- Add unit tests for each engine in `lib/engines/__tests__/`
+- Update i18n: en, pl, de, es
+
+Deliverables for a feature slice:
+- Entity/migration if persistence changes
+- API route + zod validators + openapi export
+- Backend page under `backend/sales_forecasting/`
+- Tests + `yarn workspace @open-mercato/sales-forecasting test`
+```
+
+## Changelog
+
+- **2026-05-24** — Initial spec + MVP package (`@open-mercato/sales-forecasting`): engines, predict API, runs list, admin page, migration.
