+# Sales Forecasting Package — Agent Guidelines
+
+Use `@open-mercato/sales-forecasting` for revenue time-series aggregation, forecasting engines, and forecast run persistence.
+
+## MUST Rules
+
+1. **MUST require the `sales` module** — historical series are built from `SalesOrder`; do not duplicate order tables.
+2. **MUST scope every query by `tenantId` and `organizationId`** — use `api/helpers.ts` request scope resolution.
+3. **MUST add new engines via `lib/engines/registry.ts`** — routes and services call the registry, not engine implementations directly.
+4. **MUST keep engines pure** — no database access inside `lib/engines/*`; pass `TimeSeriesPoint[]` only.
+5. **MUST add unit tests** for each engine under `lib/engines/__tests__/`.
+6. **MUST update i18n** in `en`, `pl`, `de`, `es` when adding user-facing strings.
+
+## Structure
+
+```text
+packages/sales-forecasting/src/modules/sales_forecasting/
+├── api/                      # predict + runs list
+├── backend/sales_forecasting/ # Admin UI
+├── data/                     # Entities and validators
+├── lib/engines/              # Forecast engine registry
+├── lib/aggregateSalesHistory.ts
+├── services/forecastService.ts
+└── migrations/
+```
+
+## Checklist
+
+1. Read `.ai/specs/2026-05-24-sales-forecasting-module-starter-prompt.md`
+2. Implement engine + tests
+3. `yarn workspace @open-mercato/sales-forecasting test`
+4. `yarn workspace @open-mercato/sales-forecasting build`
+5. Enable module in `apps/mercato/src/modules.ts` if not already present
